  "description": "Project J.A.R.V.I.S. is a 24-hour industry-focused hackathon conducted as part of IGNITRRON’26, where participants collaborate in teams to transform real-world problem statements into innovative, functional technology solutions. Eligibility : Open to student participants with an interest in technology, innovation, and problem-solving. Teams must consist of 2 to 4 members. Interdisciplinary teams are strongly encouraged, with skills across Full-Stack Development, AI/ML, Cloud, Cybersecurity, UI/UX, and related domains. Solo participation is not permitted. Hackathon Format Participants will select a problem statement and work intensively throughout the 24-hour challenge to research, design, develop, test, and present their solution. Teams are expected to demonstrate both technical implementation and the real-world relevance of their proposed solution. What Participants Can Expect Industry-oriented problem statements 24 hours of hands-on development and innovation Opportunities to work with modern technologies and open-source/AI tools Mentorship and guidance during the hackathon Technical evaluation and judging Live product demonstration and final presentation Recognition and certificates for participants Judging Projects will be evaluated based on factors such as problem understanding, innovation, technical implementation, functionality, usability, scalability, real-world impact, and the quality of the final demonstration. The hackathon is designed to challenge participants to think beyond conventional solutions, work effectively under time constraints, and build meaningful technology that addresses practical industry problems. Build. Innovate. Solve. Ship. PROJECT J.A.R.V.I.S. — Your 24-hour mission begins here.",
