    "details": "<p>Project J.A.R.V.I.S. is a 24-hour industry-focused hackathon conducted as part of IGNITRRON&rsquo;26, where participants collaborate in teams to transform real-world problem statements into innovative, functional technology solutions.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to student participants with an interest in technology, innovation, and problem-solving.</li>\n<li>Teams must consist of 2 to 4 members.</li>\n<li>Interdisciplinary teams are strongly encouraged, with skills across Full-Stack Development, AI/ML, Cloud, Cybersecurity, UI/UX, and related domains.</li>\n<li>Solo participation is not permitted.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Format</strong></p>\n<p>Participants will select a problem statement and work intensively throughout the 24-hour challenge to research, design, develop, test, and present their solution. Teams are expected to demonstrate both technical implementation and the real-world relevance of their proposed solution.</p>\n<p><strong>What Participants Can Expect</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Industry-oriented problem statements</li>\n<li>24 hours of hands-on development and innovation</li>\n<li>Opportunities to work with modern technologies and open-source/AI tools</li>\n<li>Mentorship and guidance during the hackathon</li>\n<li>Technical evaluation and judging</li>\n<li>Live product demonstration and final presentation</li>\n<li>Recognition and certificates for participants</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging</strong></p>\n<p>Projects will be evaluated based on factors such as problem understanding, innovation, technical implementation, functionality, usability, scalability, real-world impact, and the quality of the final demonstration.</p>\n<p>The hackathon is designed to challenge participants to think beyond conventional solutions, work effectively under time constraints, and build meaningful technology that addresses practical industry problems.</p>\n<p><strong>Build. Innovate. Solve. Ship.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PROJECT J.A.R.V.I.S. &mdash; Your 24-hour mission begins here.</strong></p>",
